---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, breadcrumbListLd, ldJson } from '../lib/seo';

// Written from what this site actually does, verified against the built output:
// a Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon (cookieless), Mapbox tiles loaded only when
// a map renders, Google Forms for the three submission forms, self-hosted fonts
// (no Google Fonts CDN), no cookies or localStorage set by the site itself, and
// static hosting on GitHub Pages. If any of that changes, this page must change
// with it — a privacy policy that describes a site you no longer run is worse
// than none at all.
const CONTACT = 'slabsavvycpa@gmail.com';
const UPDATED = '2026-07-29';

const title = 'Privacy Policy';
const description =
  'What this site collects, what it does not, and who else sees your data when you use it — written from what the site actually does.';
const pagePath = '/privacy/';

const breadcrumbLd = breadcrumbListLd([
  { name: 'Home', url: absoluteUrl(Astro.site, '/') },
  { name: 'Privacy', url: absoluteUrl(Astro.site, pagePath) },
]);
---
<Base title={`${title} | Sports Cards Near Me`} description={description}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={ldJson(breadcrumbLd)} />

  <nav class="mt-10 text-sm text-muted"><a href="/" class="hover:text-paper">Home</a> / Privacy</nav>
  <h1 class="mt-3 text-5xl md:text-7xl">Privacy</h1>
  <div class="refractor-rule mt-4 w-28"></div>

  <div class="mt-8 max-w-prose space-y-6 text-paper/90">
    <p data-answer-capsule>
      Sports Cards Near Me does not set cookies, does not run advertising, does not have user accounts, and does not
      sell or share data with anyone. It uses a privacy-first analytics tool that counts visits without identifying
      visitors. If you submit one of our forms or email us, we keep what you send so we can act on it.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">Last updated {UPDATED}.</p>

    <h2 class="text-3xl">What this site does not do</h2>
    <p>
      No cookies are set by this site. There are no accounts, no logins, and no advertising or ad-tech trackers.
      Nothing you do here is sold, rented, or shared with a data broker, and there is no email list to be added to.
      Fonts are served from this site rather than a font CDN, so loading a page does not announce your visit to a
      third-party font provider.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-3xl">Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses Cloudflare Web Analytics. It counts page views and rough traffic patterns without cookies and
      without building a profile of you — it is specifically designed not to identify individual visitors, and we
      cannot use it to single anyone out. That is why it was chosen over the more common alternatives.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-3xl">The map</h2>
    <p>
      Pages with an interactive map load it from Mapbox, and only when such a page is opened. Loading map tiles
      means Mapbox receives your IP address and the map area being viewed, the same as any embedded map. If you
      never open a page with a map, Mapbox is never contacted. Their handling of that request is governed by
      Mapbox's own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-3xl">Forms</h2>
    <p>
      The suggest-a-store, add-a-show, and verified-reseller forms are Google Forms. Anything you type into them
      goes to Google and then into a private spreadsheet only I can see. What is collected is what the form asks
      for — typically a business name, address, and contact details — plus, on some forms, your email address so a
      submission can be followed up on. Google's own privacy policy covers their part of that.
    </p>
    <p>
      Submitting a shop or show means asking for it to be published, so the business details you send are intended
      to appear publicly. Your email address is not published. The verified-reseller form is different: it exists
      specifically to publish a profile, so what appears on the resellers page is what that person asked to have
      shown there.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-3xl">Email</h2>
    <p>
      If you email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`} class="text-prizm">{CONTACT}</a>, I keep the message so I can
      reply and act on it. Nothing else happens to it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-3xl">Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      The site is static and hosted on GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub receives the requests needed to serve
      a page, including your IP address, and handles those under its own terms. There is no database here and no
      server-side code that stores anything about you.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-3xl">Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      This directory links out to shops' own websites and social pages, ticket platforms, and grading companies.
      Once you follow a link, you are on their site under their rules — nothing in this policy applies there.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-3xl">Your requests</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`} class="text-prizm">{CONTACT}</a> and I will act on it. Shop owners can ask
      to have a listing corrected or removed entirely, no reason required. If you have submitted a form and want
      what you sent deleted, say so and it will be deleted. Under Canadian privacy law (PIPEDA) you can also ask
      what personal information is held about you; given how little this site collects, the honest answer is usually
      "nothing beyond a form you filled in."
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-3xl">Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If what the site collects ever changes, this page changes with it and the date above is updated. See{' '}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-prizm">the About page</a> for who runs this directory, where listings come from,
      and how corrections work.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
